Next up are leftanti joins. The leftanti join finds things that DON'T exist. It returns left rows (from the original table) with NO match in the right table (the one we are joining). We are given:
Employees
| join kind=leftanti (
    AuthenticationEvents
    | where timestamp between (datetime(2025-06-01) .. datetime(2025-06-07))
) on $left.username == $right.username
This finds employees with no login activity in the week of June 1st. Here, it will return rows from the Employees table, but no additional info from from the Authentication Events table. The AuthenticationEvents table is solely used for filtering.

Someone in our company has no Authentication data at all. Use leftanti to find them. What is the name of the employee with no auth data?
Use the previous query, and take out the timestamp filtering.
Answer: Jason Chen

